def bellman_ford(n, edges, src):
    INF=float('inf')
    dist=[INF]*n; dist[src]=0
    for _ in range(n-1):
        for u,v,w in edges:
            if dist[u]+w<dist[v]: dist[v]=dist[u]+w
    # negative cycle detection
    for u,v,w in edges:
        if dist[u]+w<dist[v]: return None  # negative cycle reachable
    return dist
```
O(V·E). After V-1 relaxations all shortest paths converge if no negative cycle. The V-th pass detects negative cycles.

