def quickselect(a, k):
    a=list(a)
    def mom(arr):
        if len(arr)<=5: return sorted(arr)[len(arr)//2]
        groups=[arr[i:i+5] for i in range(0,len(arr),5)]
        meds=[sorted(g)[len(g)//2] for g in groups]
        return mom(meds)
    def select(arr,k):
        if len(arr)==1: return arr[0]
        piv=mom(arr)
        lo=[x for x in arr if x<piv]
        hi=[x for x in arr if x>piv]
        eq=[x for x in arr if x==piv]
        if k<len(lo): return select(lo,k)
        if k<len(lo)+len(eq): return piv
        return select(hi,k-len(lo)-len(eq))
    return select(a,k)
```
Median-of-medians guarantees the pivot eliminates ≥ 30% of elements → T(n)=T(n/5)+T(7n/10)+O(n) → O(n) worst case.

